    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Improve memory locality and loop order by using a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks, ensuring correct boundary handling.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\"Reorganize the matrix processing into blocks\", \"Adjust loop orders for better cache performance\"],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <climits>\\n\\nint main() {\\n\\tint n, s;\\n\\tstd::cin >> n >> s;\\n\\tstd::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n\\tfor (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n\\t\\tfor (int j = 0; j < n; j++) \\n\\t\\t\\tscanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n\\tassert(s < n);\\n\\tassert(n < 8000);\\n\\tassert(s > 0);\\n\\tassert(n > 0);\\n\\n\\tconst int blockSize = 32; // Define a block size for better cache performance\\n\\tint mxSum = INT_MIN;\\n\\n\\tfor (int bi = 0; bi <= n - s; bi += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\tfor (int bj = 0; bj <= n - s; bj += blockSize) {\\n\\t\\t\\tint sum = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\tfor (int i = bi; i < std::min(bi + blockSize, n - s + 1); ++i) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int j = bj; j < std::min(bj + blockSize, n - s + 1); ++j) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum = 0;\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int ii = i; ii < i + s; ++ii) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tfor (int jj = j; jj < j + s; ++jj) {\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tsum += matrix[ii][jj];\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t\\tmxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n\\t\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t\\t}\\n\\t\\t}\\n\\t}\\n\\n\\tprintf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"This experiment introduces a blocked approach to process submatrices in larger chunks, which can improve memory locality and cache performance. The block size is set to 32, but this can be tuned based on the specific hardware characteristics.\"\n}"
